      "description": "Named by value because that is what they are; the role names are the semantic layer's job. TWO LADDERS, one grid. The document ladder (11…64) is what the case studies, the resume panel and the work index render. The landing ladder (10…56) runs ~12.5% under it, rung for rung, and exists because the homepage sets its type in a 492px measure against a full-bleed canvas — the document sizes read as shouting there. Both are real and shipped; neither is a scaled-down copy the browser could compute, because the rounding was chosen by eye per rung (16→14, not 16→14.0). Every size below is consumed through a --text-* role in the semantic layer. Nothing should reference --size-* directly."
